body:
We are huge fans of `p-retry`! We're using it in a bunch of places in our codebase and we found something we think may be a bug.

Here is a minimal repro that mimics our code:
```
import pRetry from "p-retry";

const signal = AbortSignal.timeout(1_000);
pRetry(
  async () => {
    console.log("running input function");
    const { promise, reject } = Promise.withResolvers();
    signal.addEventListener(
      "abort",
      () => {
        reject(signal.reason);
      },
      { once: true }
    );
    await promise;
  },
  {
    minTimeout: 10_000,
    signal,
    unref: true,
  }
)
  .catch((err) => {
    console.log("caught error:", err);
  })
  .finally(() => {
    console.log("finally");
  });
console.log("sleeping for 5 seconds");
await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 5_000));
console.log("Done");
```

When the AbortSignal is aborted we expected the retry loop to immediately stop and print "finally". However what we see with this code is that the "finally" isn't printed until after the retry timeout expires. For now we can workaround the issue with code like this:
```
shouldRetry: () => !signal.aborted,
```

One possible fix would be to add code like this around line 144:
```
options.signal?.throwIfAborted(); // this is a new line of code
options.signal?.addEventListener('abort', onAbort, {once: true});
```

From the docs, it is unclear to me whether `shouldRetry` _replaces_ any retry logic imposed by `options.retries`, `options.maxTimeout`, or if those still apply.


By example, does `retries: 5` have any affect here? I suspect it does, but that isn't clear to me.

```js
import pRetry from 'p-retry';

const run = async () => { … };

const result = await pRetry(run, {
        retries: 5,
	shouldRetry: ({error, attemptNumber, retriesLeft}) => !(error instanceof CustomError)
});
```

I'm asking because I'm looking for a way to "skip" a given request, conditionally based on the response/error. `hono-rate-limiter` has `skip` option for this: https://github.com/rhinobase/hono-rate-limiter/blob/main/packages/cloudflare/src/types.ts#L75

